        <!-- Terroir Explanation -->
        <div class="terroir-explanation">
            <h4>🌍 Understanding Terroir</h4>
            <p><strong>Terroir</strong> is the complete environmental context that influences coffee flavor: soil composition, climate, altitude, rainfall patterns, temperature variations, and even the surrounding ecosystem. Just like wine, coffee reflects its place of origin.</p>
            <p>In Peru, the combination of high altitudes, volcanic soils, and microclimates creates unique flavor profiles that can't be replicated anywhere else in the world. Each farm, each micro-lot, tells a story of its specific terroir.</p>
